// Bans the `as unknown as T` double-cast in production TypeScript.
//
// The double cast is TypeScript's "type system blind spot" — it silences the
// compiler without runtime safety. Prefer a type guard (`"key" in obj`,
// `typeof x === ...`), a Zod parse at the boundary, or narrowing at the
// source. Library type gaps (dockerode hijacked streams, AI-SDK provider
// extensions, etc.) keep the cast — add `// biome-ignore lint/plugin/no-unsafe-cast: <gap>`
// on the line above and name the upstream type gap.
//
// Test files are exempt: stubbing partial interfaces is the dominant use and
// `mock<T>()` / `mockDeep<T>()` from vitest-mock-extended is the preferred
// replacement (see .claude/rules/testing.md).
//
// The exemption is a substring match on `.test.` and `/test/`, which tracks
// the project's actual layout (`*.test.ts` suffix + `src/test/` helper
// directory). Revisit if the test layout shifts to `__tests__/` or `tests/`
// — both forms would slip through today. The smoke test in
// `src/test/biome-plugin.test.ts` covers the positive, negative, and
// suppression-comment paths.

language js

`$x as unknown as $y` as $node where {
  $filename <: not includes ".test.",
  $filename <: not includes "/test/",
  register_diagnostic(span=$node, message="Avoid `as unknown as`. Use a type guard (`in`, `typeof`), Zod parse, or narrow at the source. For genuine upstream type gaps, add `// biome-ignore lint/plugin/no-unsafe-cast: <reason>` on the line above.")
}
